# Shell scripts must keep LF line endings — bash on Linux refuses CRLF.
# Without this, the autocrlf=true that Git for Windows ships by default
# would rewrite checkouts to CRLF and ./start.sh on the VPS would fail
# with `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env^M: no such file or directory`.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Windows .bat files MUST keep CRLF endings. cmd.exe parses .bat under the
# assumption every line ends with CRLF; an LF-only file makes cmd glue
# REM comments together and treat them as commands ("'Pre-IPO' is not
# recognized as an internal or external command"). The Edit tool can
# silently strip CRLF when modifying these files on a Linux-style shell,
# so we force CRLF on checkout to make the foot-gun unreachable.
*.bat text eol=crlf
